# Example weekly re-crawl schedule for the 12 in-scope sites.
#
# Install by copying into a real crontab (after setting REPO_DIR below):
#   crontab crontab.example
# or merge these lines into an existing one via `crontab -e`.
#
# Design
# ------
# At most 2 crawls run at once (leaves headroom for a manual `crawl`/
# `crawl-and-push` on top of the schedule). Each weekday below fires two
# buckets in parallel; sites *within* one bucket run sequentially, one
# after another. The two largest, most memory-hungry sites
# (georgewbush_whitehouse, obama_whitehouse) run alongside much smaller
# sites so there is less competition for resources.
# Every site is crawled with --download-delay 2 and
# --concurrent-requests-per-domain 1 - one request every 2 seconds, no
# concurrent connections to the same target. That's a deliberate
# compromise: faster than several of these sites' own robots.txt
# Crawl-delay (10s for CW1-6/open_obama_whitehouse/trumpwhitehouse), but
# far gentler than settings.py's local default (0.25s/4 concurrent).
#
# Approximate bucket durations at that 2s/1-connection rate, and the
# buffer before the next scheduled day:
#   Sun bucket A: georgewbush_whitehouse alone             ~46h    (buffer to Wed: ~26h)
#   Sun bucket B: open_obama_whitehouse, letsmove          ~1h05m
#   Wed bucket A: obama_whitehouse alone                   ~30h10m (buffer to Fri: ~17h50m)
#   Wed bucket B: trumpwhitehouse, bidenwhitehouse          ~12h57m
#   Fri bucket A: clintonwhitehouse1-6, sequential          ~34h17m (buffer to Sun: ~13h43m)
#   Fri bucket B: (empty placeholder for a future site)
#
# Per-site CSV/harvest/exclusions output and ErrorFileLogger's ERROR-level
# log are all written automatically by the pipeline regardless of this
# file - nothing here needs to arrange that. The data/cron-*.log files
# below are just a combined stdout/stderr trace per bucket, so a failed
# run's traceback is somewhere durable instead of vanishing into cron's
# own mail handling.
#
# push.py (see archive_crawler/pipeline/push.py) uploads for real -
# `crawl-and-push` below validates/filters/converts every site on
# schedule, then uploads its JSONL to S3. Requires AWS credentials to be
# resolvable on this server (real AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID/etc. environment
# variables, or a .env file per .env.example) and NARA_S3_BUCKET set;
# missing either fails that job with a clear error rather than crawling
# for nothing. Switch to plain `crawl` instead if a schedule that only
# crawls/validates without uploading is wanted.
#
# Every job invokes the venv's own python3 directly (rather than relying
# on PATH or scrape_index_pipeline's #!/usr/bin/env python3 shebang) -
# cron's own PATH is minimal and won't include this project's venv, and
# cron's top-of-file KEY=value lines are parsed literally, not expanded,
# so a $REPO_DIR reference inside one of those (e.g. in a PATH= line)
# would NOT work. $REPO_DIR only expands correctly inside a job's own
# command line below, which cron runs via a real shell.

REPO_DIR=/home/scrapy/nara-scrapy-crawler
SHELL=/bin/sh

# --- Sunday ---------------------------------------------------------------

# Bucket A: georgewbush_whitehouse (alone - largest/most memory-hungry site)
0 0 * * 0 cd "$REPO_DIR" && ./venv/bin/python3 ./scrape_index_pipeline crawl-and-push georgewbush_whitehouse --download-delay 2 --concurrent-requests-per-domain 1 >> "$REPO_DIR/data/cron-sun-a-georgewbush.log" 2>&1

# Bucket B: the two smallest sites, sequential
0 0 * * 0 cd "$REPO_DIR" && ( ./venv/bin/python3 ./scrape_index_pipeline crawl-and-push open_obama_whitehouse --download-delay 2 --concurrent-requests-per-domain 1; ./venv/bin/python3 ./scrape_index_pipeline crawl-and-push letsmove --download-delay 2 --concurrent-requests-per-domain 1 ) >> "$REPO_DIR/data/cron-sun-b-small-sites.log" 2>&1

# --- Wednesday --------------------------------------------------------------

# Bucket A: obama_whitehouse (alone - second-largest/memory-hungry site)
0 0 * * 3 cd "$REPO_DIR" && ./venv/bin/python3 ./scrape_index_pipeline crawl-and-push obama_whitehouse --download-delay 2 --concurrent-requests-per-domain 1 >> "$REPO_DIR/data/cron-wed-a-obamawhitehouse.log" 2>&1

# Bucket B: trumpwhitehouse, bidenwhitehouse, sequential
0 0 * * 3 cd "$REPO_DIR" && ( ./venv/bin/python3 ./scrape_index_pipeline crawl-and-push trumpwhitehouse --download-delay 2 --concurrent-requests-per-domain 1; ./venv/bin/python3 ./scrape_index_pipeline crawl-and-push bidenwhitehouse --download-delay 2 --concurrent-requests-per-domain 1 ) >> "$REPO_DIR/data/cron-wed-b-trump-biden.log" 2>&1

# --- Friday -----------------------------------------------------------------

# Bucket A: all six Clinton sites, sequential
0 0 * * 5 cd "$REPO_DIR" && ( ./venv/bin/python3 ./scrape_index_pipeline crawl-and-push clintonwhitehouse1 --download-delay 2 --concurrent-requests-per-domain 1; ./venv/bin/python3 ./scrape_index_pipeline crawl-and-push clintonwhitehouse2 --download-delay 2 --concurrent-requests-per-domain 1; ./venv/bin/python3 ./scrape_index_pipeline crawl-and-push clintonwhitehouse3 --download-delay 2 --concurrent-requests-per-domain 1; ./venv/bin/python3 ./scrape_index_pipeline crawl-and-push clintonwhitehouse4 --download-delay 2 --concurrent-requests-per-domain 1; ./venv/bin/python3 ./scrape_index_pipeline crawl-and-push clintonwhitehouse5 --download-delay 2 --concurrent-requests-per-domain 1; ./venv/bin/python3 ./scrape_index_pipeline crawl-and-push clintonwhitehouse6 --download-delay 2 --concurrent-requests-per-domain 1 ) >> "$REPO_DIR/data/cron-fri-a-clinton-sites.log" 2>&1

# Bucket B: placeholder for a future site - uncomment and fill in once one exists
# 0 0 * * 5 cd "$REPO_DIR" && ./venv/bin/python3 ./scrape_index_pipeline crawl-and-push NEW_SITE_NAME --download-delay 2 --concurrent-requests-per-domain 1 >> "$REPO_DIR/data/cron-fri-b-placeholder.log" 2>&1
